To build your very first machine as a lone human, you must look past modern electronics and focus on mechanical advantage. A machine is simply any device that multiplies, redirects, or transforms human force to do work.
Your first machine will be a Lathe with a Foot Treadle and Flywheel. This machine is historically known as the "Mother of Tools" because it allows you to rotate a piece of wood or metal at high speeds, using sharp stone or bronze chisels to carve perfectly symmetrical, circular components. With a lathe, you can manufacture axles, gears, pulleys, and pistons, unlocking the entire Industrial Age.
Here is how you build it using the materials you’ve already mastered (stone tools, rope, high-heat kilns, and copper/bronze).
------------------------------
## The Anatomy of the Foot-Powered Lathe
The machine uses a foot pedal to pull a rope, which spins a drive shaft. A heavy stone or clay disk (the flywheel) keeps the shaft spinning smoothly between pedal pumps, converting uneven leg motion into smooth, continuous rotational energy.

